Every boulder you destroy in Sokoban, brings your luck one point down.
And during full moon, the base luck is one point higher than other times.
So, if you broke one of the boulders, it was compensated by the moon phase
for a while, but not after the full moon phase ended. (Or, after you saved
the game and continued after the full moon phase. The game only checks the
moon phase at the beginning of the game and when you restore a saved
game.)
And if you broke two of them, that had more effect than full moon. 
So wand of striking was not the best possible option, but if it was the
only one available, you didn't have too many options.
Good and bad luck time out anyway unless you're carrying a luckstone, so
the penalty is not permanent (unless you get killed before it times out).

